---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { pageTitle } from '../lib/seo';
---
<BaseLayout title={pageTitle('Privacy')} description="How Sunnie Designs handles your data: what we collect when you order, who processes it, and the two strictly necessary cookies we use.">
  <article class="container narrow prose">
    <header class="page-head"><h1>Privacy notice</h1></header>
    <p>Last updated: September 2026.</p>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Sunnie Designs sells handmade crochet pieces. Contact us about privacy at <a href={`mailto:${site.email.hello}`}>{site.email.hello}</a>.</p>
    <p>
      The data controller for this website is {site.company.legalName}, trading as {site.company.tradingAs}. CRO
      {' '}{site.company.cro}. Registered office: {site.company.registeredOffice}. Email:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email.hello}`}>{site.email.hello}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>What this website collects</h2>
    <p>
      This site runs no tracking or advertising scripts. Cloudflare, our host, keeps standard server logs and
      aggregate visit counts. Nothing in these identifies you.
    </p>
    <h2>When you order</h2>
    <p>
      When you buy on sunniedesigns.com, we collect your name, email address, delivery address and what you
      bought, to fulfil your order and send you order updates.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you start a checkout but don't complete payment, the details you entered are stored with the unpaid
      order record. We delete unpaid order records after 90 days.
    </p>
    <h2>Our lawful basis</h2>
    <p>
      We process your order data because it's necessary to perform the contract between us: taking your order,
      charging you and delivering your pieces. We keep order records afterwards to meet our legal obligations,
      including Irish tax record-keeping rules, which require us to keep them for 6 years.
    </p>
    <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
    <p>
      PayPal processes your payment details as an independent controller, under its own privacy statement, not on
      our instructions. Resend, which sends our order emails, and Cloudflare, which hosts the site and stores the
      order database, act as processors on our behalf.
    </p>
    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Some of these providers may process your data outside the European Economic Area. Where that happens, they
      do so under the European Commission's standard contractual clauses or an adequacy decision.
    </p>
    <h2>How long we keep order records</h2>
    <p>We keep order records for 6 years, to meet Irish tax rules.</p>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      We use two strictly necessary cookies: one to remember what's in your bag, and one to show your order
      confirmation. We set no tracking or advertising cookies.
    </p>
    <h2>Emails you send us</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we use your address and message only to reply, and we delete them when we no longer need them.</p>
    <h2>Orders on Etsy</h2>
    <p>Purchases placed on our Etsy shop are handled by Etsy, under Etsy's privacy policy.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you can ask to see, correct or delete data we hold about you. Email us and we'll respond within a
      month. You can also complain to the Irish Data Protection Commission.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
